WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.170
BRICS has 11 members,
including China and Russia.

2
00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:07.090
In 2026, India chairs it.

3
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:12.530
Since 2017, it has been a full member of
the Shanghai Cooperation Organisation.

4
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:16.950
Yet it is also in the Quad, a
diplomatic partnership with Australia,

5
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.110
Japan and the USA.

6
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:25.890
Exports grew from 7 per cent of
GDP in 1990 to 22 per cent in 2025.

7
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.950
So how do friendships with rival
powers shape its development?

8
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.290
Is it drifting to one side?

9
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.050
Do friendships not matter?

10
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:39.310
In this mission, you'll map how India's
top trade partners changed in twenty years.

11
00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.850
Then you'll judge how these ties
help or hold back its development.

12
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:48.340
Your mission: explain how India's
friendships shape its development.
